        "id": 43819,
        "name": "lynkfox",
        "username": "lynkfox",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/lynkfox/{size}/1997_2.png",
        "created_at": "2012-11-14T22:48:51.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Ameena\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/ameena/48/1907_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Ameena:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Bann Sidhe…is that a deliberate pun on \"banshee\", because that's how I'd pronounce it…</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>As explained int he post above thats how it was originally spelled (well bean sidhe) until it was redone later. So its nota&nbsp; deliberate pun, but Banshee comes from the word bean sidhe, an english derivative of it I guess.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>And cool to know on spelling changes. Learn something new every day</p>",
