      {
        "id": 43820,
        "name": "Katsue",
        "username": "Katsue",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/katsue/{size}/2012_2.png",
        "created_at": "2012-11-14T23:23:00.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"lynkfox\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/lynkfox/48/1997_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> lynkfox:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<div><b>Ameena wrote:</b><br><blockquote>Bann Sidhe...is that a deliberate pun on \"banshee\", because that's how I'd pronounce it...\n&nbsp;\n</blockquote></div>\n&nbsp;As explained int he post above thats how it was originally spelled (well bean sidhe) until it was redone later. So its nota&nbsp; deliberate pun, but Banshee comes from the word bean sidhe, an english derivative of it I guess.&nbsp;And cool to know on spelling changes. Learn something new every day\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Banshee and <em>bean sidhe</em> have pretty much the same pronunciation, with perhaps a slight shift of emphasis. And yeah, banshee is just an English transliteration of <em>bean sidhe</em>.</p>",
